# Branch protection requires an approval from an owner of every path a
# pull request touches (see scripts/configure-repository.sh). Patterns
# are matched top to bottom and the last match wins, so the CI/CD rules
# below override the general one for the paths they name.
#
# GitHub never lets the author of a pull request satisfy this with their
# own approval. A path whose only owner is also its author has nobody
# left who can approve it — worth remembering before narrowing one.

# General code
* @allowyoba @kcamapaaa @o000oo799

# CI/CD, release and deployment
/.github/ @allowyoba
/ansible/ @allowyoba
/docker/ @allowyoba
/scripts/ @allowyoba
/Makefile @allowyoba
/release.config.mjs @allowyoba
/package.json @allowyoba
/package-lock.json @allowyoba
